course: dictionary
lesson: 5762
title: Lukewarm: not hot, not cold
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a point in the middle. Lukewarm is one of them. It means only slightly warm, not hot and not cold. «Lukewarm water» is the kind you might use for a baby's bath.
explain: Lukewarm can also describe a feeling about people or things. «The new pupil got a lukewarm welcome» means the other children were not very friendly or excited. The clue is in the words around it: a welcome is usually warm, so a lukewarm one is less warm than you would expect.
explain: Your skin judges temperature by change, not just by the number. «Skin judges hot and cold by change: after warm water, lukewarm water feels cool, and after cold water, the same lukewarm water feels warm.» So the same water can feel cool or warm, depending on what touched your skin before.
fact: Lukewarm means only slightly warm, not hot and not cold.
fact: «Lukewarm water» is a good temperature for a baby's bath.
fact: For a burn, use cool running water, not lukewarm water.
fact: «Lukewarm» can also mean not very interested or excited, as in «a lukewarm response».
fact: The same lukewarm water can feel cool after warm water and warm after cold water, because your skin notices change.
exercise: What does lukewarm mean? | Freezing cold, with ice in it | Boiling hot, with steam rising | *Only slightly warm, not hot and not cold
exercise: «The crowd gave the new band a lukewarm response.» What does lukewarm suggest? | Very excited and loud | *Not very excited | Angry and shouting
exercise: Which water is best for a baby's bath? | *Lukewarm water | Boiling water | Ice-cold water
test: «After the cold swim, the lukewarm water felt warm.» Why did it feel warm? | Because lukewarm water is always boiling | *Because your skin had been cold, so lukewarm water feels warm by comparison | Because lukewarm means very hot
test: Ella says, «This lukewarm tea is disappointing.» What does lukewarm tea mean? | *Tea that is only slightly warm | Tea that has been iced and is very cold | Tea that is boiling and bubbling
exam: «The teacher gave a lukewarm welcome to the new pupil.» What does lukewarm suggest here? | Icy cold, with snow on the floor | *Not very friendly or excited | Very warm and welcoming | Shouting loudly
